# Academic contents — this repository holds the system and never the coursework the system
# organises (docs/adr/0002). Blunt on purpose: the failure it exists to prevent is one `git add -A`
# away, and it is not recallable from a public repository. A file that genuinely belongs here and
# is refused by these rules is added with `git add -f`, and the pull request says why.
